Author: Mesquita <mesquita@aospa.co>
Date:   Thu Nov 23 21:34:34 2023 -0300

    Settings: Fix a null pointer exception on cutout force full screen

     * When orientation change occurs, android restarts the running Activity
       (onDestroy() is called, followed by onCreate()).
       That was causing DisplayCutoutForceFullscreen to crash due to
       appBarLayout being null after the screen rotation.
       Using lazy instead of lateinit will help to avoid this issue.

    Change-Id: Ib2ae298978bbfe5eb3defcabd013e86a5442961b
    Signed-off-by: Mesquita <mesquita@aospa.co>

[ghostrider-reborn]
- Improve layout, don't show package name
- Use background thread for loading the apps list
- Cleanup unused variables and run ktfmt
